        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zeros of the function are $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$.\n- **II.** The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{3π}{2} + 2nπ$.\n- **III.** The range of $y = \\cos x$ is $[- 1, 0]$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Cosine has zeros at x=pi/2+n*pi. At x=3pi/2+2n*pi it is zero, not maximal, and its range is [-1,1]. Only I is true."
