        ":question/id": "4817b633-1cdd-52d9-b9a7-098236a7867f",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-103230",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n- **II.** Its range is $y\\in [-2,2]$\n- **III.** $y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is an output of the function",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, the function $y=cos⁡x$ takes the value zero.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. The range of the function $y=cos⁡x$ is $y\\in [-1,1].$ Thus, $y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is not an output of this function."
      },
