        ":question/id": "4afb86c8-970f-594e-bb88-36f6e2c3e725",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-103233",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $\n- **II.** Its graph passes through the point $(0,1)$\n- **III.** The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=0,$ the function has the value $y=cos⁡0=1.$ Therefore, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$"
      },
