        ":question/id": "69137884-05b3-53be-9c7c-95b53b1ed329",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-27009",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- **II.** The function has a minimum value at  $x=2\\pi .$\n\n- **III.** The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=0.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/9c/9c77bec4ebb04668fbff5176418ed9c09143a8660879fdf523a158c5f109006c.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a maximum at $x=2\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$"
