        ":question/id": "f5773d37-2017-53ae-a0d1-64c772d0dcaf",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-70666",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$\n- **II.** The function is zero at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"
      },
