        ":question/id": "24b90149-221d-555e-91aa-b1d1cb7cb1c0",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-70667",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1$\n\n- **II.** The function has a minimum value at $x=-\\pi .$\n\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The $y$-intercepts of the function is $y=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function at $x=-\\pi $ has a minimum value.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"
